## TL;DR — Men's 2 Carat Diamond Ring in 60 Seconds

**5 rules that separate a smart 2ct buy from an expensive mistake:**

1. **Band width floor rises.** 2ct = 8.1mm stone. You need 6mm minimum, 7–8mm ideal.
2. **G is the correct color.** At 2ct face-up, G is visually colorless in white or yellow gold. F and E add $2,000+ for a difference no one sees.
3. **VS2 is mandatory.** At 8.1mm face-up, inclusions are more visible than at 1ct. No SI1.
4. **Excellent cut only.** At 2ct, cut quality is visible from across a table. Very Good shows.
5. **Check the lab gap first.** A 2ct IGI lab-grown G-VS2 runs $2,000–$3,000. A GIA natural runs $16,490+. That is a $13,000+ gap. Decide which side you are on before you pick a setting.

→ Entry solitaire: **[Grooved Solitaire WG $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-tapered-grooved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147386?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** + **[GIA G-VS2 2ct $16,490](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29307739?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** = **$17,490**

→ Channel band (complete, no stone): **[Channel Set 6mm WG — $830](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/channel-set-mens-diamond-wedding-band-in-14k-white-gold-600mm-by-james-allen-item-305355?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

→ Statement pick: **[Geometric Channel YG $1,410](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/geometric-channel-mens-diamond-wedding-band-in-14k-yellow-gold-650mm-by-james-allen-item-305350?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** + **[GIA G-VS2 2ct $16,490](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29307739?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** = **$17,900**

