## The Men's Grade Floor at 2ct — What GIA Says Changes

[GIA](https://www.gia.edu/diamond-quality-factor) grades every natural diamond on the 4Cs. At 2ct, the grade floor is stricter than at 1ct. The stone is 60% larger face-up. Every grade decision shows more.

**Color:** G is the floor. At 2ct, H reads warm in white gold or platinum. The face-up area is large enough that body color shows. In yellow gold, H works. In white metal, H reads off-white. G is safe in any metal. F and E add $1,650–$5,000 over G at equal clarity. No visible return.

**Clarity:** VS2 minimum. No exceptions at 2ct. An SI1 that passes eye-clean tests at 1ct will often fail at 2ct. The face-up area is larger. The eye has more surface to scan. VS2 adds $400–$600 over SI1 at this weight. That is correct money spent.

**Cut:** Excellent only. At 8.1mm face-up, the difference between Excellent and Very Good cut is not subtle. Excellent cut fires light across a room. Very Good just sits there. GIA Excellent is non-negotiable at this carat weight.

| Grade | Natural 2ct Round | What this means |
|---|---|---|
| G-VS2 | [$16,490](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29307739?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | The correct floor. Eye-clean, colorless in any metal. |
| F-VS2 | [$18,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29142126?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $1,650 more than G-VS2 for color no one sees. |
| G-VS1 | [$22,460](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29249620?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $5,970 more than entry. One clarity step. Skip it. |
| E-VS1 | [$22,660](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493026?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $6,170 premium over G-VS2. E color at 2ct in a men's setting is wasted. |
| G-VVS2 | [$26,610](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28819967?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $10,120 premium for clarity no one sees. Only if the cert is the goal. |
| D-VS2 | [$26,490](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28720470?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $10,000 over G-VS2. D at 2ct in any men's setting is performance buying. |

**Verdict:** G-VS2 at $16,490 is the benchmark. Every grade above costs thousands more for a return you will not see in a men's setting. For a full context on how GIA grades stack up at different carat weights, see [Men's Round Diamond Ring](/mens-round-diamond-ring).

