### Setting Type 4 — Geometric / Alternative Metal (Boldest Statement)

Geometric settings wrap the center stone in a shaped frame. Think hexagonal bezels, angular channel walls, or structured cutouts. The stone sits inside the geometry, not on top of it. Alternative metals — tantalum, black titanium — add scratch resistance and a finish white gold cannot replicate.

At 2ct, a geometric frame matters more than at 1ct. The 8.1mm stone is wide enough that a plain prong head can look minimal. A geometric frame gives the stone context.

